    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "We examine the performance of liquidity proxies in commodities. The Amihud measure\nhas the largest correlation with liquidity benchmarks. Amivest and Effective Tick measures\nalso perform well. These proxies are useful for studies of commodity liquidity over a long\ntime period and those that lack access to high-frequency data. We use various aspects of\ntransaction costs, such as spread, depth, immediacy, and resiliency, to give insight into the\ncosts of different execution approaches. Transaction costs increase with volatility and exhibit\nmean reversion. Splitting trades over one hour can reduce trading costs by two-thirds\ncompared to an immediate execution.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : 0,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
